Raid_Config.RaidBoss_Option_0_Info:
{Alive Time}

This value shows how long Raid Bosses roam on the adventure map. Ideally, this value should be connected to the map layout and spawn radius.
Recommended: 10 days.

Raid_Config.RaidBoss_Option_1_Info:
{Spawn Chance}

This is the base chance of Raid Bosses spawning on the map. It increases by 1% per day until a Raid Boss appears. This means that even if you set the chance to zero, a Raid Boss will eventually appear.
Recommended: 10%.

Raid_Config.RaidBoss_Option_2_Info:
{Spawn Radius}

This is the radius around the town in which the Raid Boss can spawn. Adjusting this value for certain maps can prevent the Boss from spawning too far away.
The recommended radius is 20 tiles on the X and Y axes, depending on the map.

Raid_Config.RaidBoss_Option_3_Info:
{Spawn Cooldown}

The time before a new Raid Boss can spawn again for a player.
Recommended: 7 days.

Raid_Config.RaidBoss_Option_4_Info:
{Start Delay}

Set the number of days for which the monster will not spawn from the start of the game.
The recommended number of days is 28.
